WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.080
We knew Emperor Palpatine would be back for
months before The Rise of Skywalker ever hit

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.770
theaters, but we didn't know how or why.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.360
Now that the film is finally out, we have
the answers to some of our questions, but

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.730
it takes a little bit of consideration to
assemble that knowledge into a clear picture.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.739
Spoilers for Rise of Skywalker are, of course,
ahead.

00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:24.240
The Rise of Skywalker is a film with so much
going on that, even with Palpatine's story

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.119
at the core of it all, viewers only get pieces
of the full picture.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:32.760
It's not totally clear how he returned after
his death in Return of the Jedi.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.580
When we first meet him again on Exegol, Palpatine
is alive, but admits that he has been dead

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.580
before.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.200
His somehow even-more decrepit appearance
suggests that he's spent years hanging on

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.170
to what little life he has with the help of
machines.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:51.240
It seems Palpatine owes a great deal of his
revival to the efforts of loyal followers

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.380
who became a cult of Sith resurrectionists
bent on enacting his will through any means

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:57.660
necessary.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.070
Palpatine may have appeared as pure evil to
a great many people in the galaxy, but to

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.960
others he really was their one true leader.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.370
Thanks to them, he was recovered from the
Death Star, given some kind of new life, and

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.420
brought to the legendary Sith world.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.369
In the build-up to The Rise of Skywalker's
release, fans posited theories from cloning

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:23.139
to the "World Between Worlds" of Star Wars
Rebels as possible explanations of Palpatine's

00:01:23.139 --> 00:01:28.530
revival, but we still have neither confirmation
nor denial of any particular method.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:33.259
What we do know is that Palpatine is constantly
connected to a life support system that pumps

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.680
various liquids into and perhaps out of his
body.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:42.319
This would suggest some kind of dark scientific
method of revival, perhaps similar to Darth

00:01:42.319 --> 00:01:45.960
Vader's life support system but it's also
possible that's only one part of a bigger

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:46.960
picture.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.369
It's possible that other dark secrets, from
Sith rituals to others pieces of magic, were

00:01:51.369 --> 00:01:55.380
used to jumpstart Palpatine's livelihood again.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.289
Palpatine apparently didn't believe he could
simply announce that he'd returned and retake

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:01.590
his place at the top of the pecking order.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:06.130
Instead, he needed a puppet to function as
a disruptor for the New Republic.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.920
Enter Supreme Leader Snoke.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.360
"Our strategy must now change."

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.940
When he meets Kylo Ren, Palpatine declares
outright "I made Snoke," and then provides

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.580
evidence via a tank full of discarded Snoke
bodies.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:25.960
So, the Supreme Leader of the First Order
was, at some point, engineered and created

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:31.570
by Palpatine himself to both serve as a puppet
leader and draw the darkness out of Ben Solo.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:36.780
It worked, because Kylo Ren did rise as a
powerful follower of the Dark Side, killing

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.379
Snoke in the process.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:44.760
After his defeat at the Battle of Endor, Palpatine
no longer wanted to simply rule the galaxy.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.760
He wanted to impose a sense of fear in every
single star system.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.770
He'd need a whole fleet of planet killers.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:56.120
Palpatine and his many followers deployed
their resources to create the military machinery

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.350
of "The Final Order," a massive fleet of Star
Destroyers each equipped with a planet-killing

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.350
cannon on the underside.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:08.660
We saw "miniaturized Death Star tech" deployed
by the First Order in The Last Jedi, and in

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.900
The Rise of Skywalker, it becomes clear that
Palpatine and his followers have found a way

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:16.590
to make those tools even more deadly.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:21.070
After waiting for decades, Palpatine felt
the time was right to make his move with Kylo

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.460
Ren in place as the First Order's Supreme
Leader.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:28.950
But Palpatine couldn't just leave his life
support machinery in his fortress on Exegol,

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.890
and perhaps he didn't want to.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.400
Instead, he sent a mysterious message to the
galaxy, in which he vowed revenge.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.560
"Did you ever hear the tragedy of Darth Plagueis
the Wise?"

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:40.680
Rumors of a resurrected Palpatine quickly
swirled, terrifying the Resistance and enraging

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.130
Kylo Ren.

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:47.210
Ren hunts down a Sith Wayfinder and seeks
out Palpatine on Exegol.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.871
Palpatine reveals to him that he was the architect
behind Snoke, and he's been the Darth Vader

00:03:51.871 --> 00:03:53.680
voice in Ren's head.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.030
He makes Kylo Ren an offer of control of the
Final Order fleet, and leadership over a new

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.180
Empire.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.490
Ren accepts the offer and agrees to Palpatine's
one condition: that Ren track down and kill

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:06.490
Rey.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:11.090
To help facilitate this, Palpatine also provides
Ren with a key piece of information that helps

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:16.840
explain why he wants her dead: Rey is Palpatine's
granddaughter, and therefore a major threat

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.350
to his plans for the return of the Empire.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:24.140
Palpatine soon begins reckoning with the other
potential threats to his plan.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:29.220
A spy within the First Order, later revealed
to be General Hux, leaks information about

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.840
the Final Order fleet to what's left of the
Resistance.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.960
Commander Poe Dameron launches a covert operation
with the hope of stopping the Final Order's

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.260
launch before it starts.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.290
Palpatine has key allies in a position to
provide help to eliminate the spy.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.889
In the Order's rise to power, Allegiant General
Pryde has emerged as a Palpatine loyalist

00:04:48.889 --> 00:04:51.200
who'd fought with him in the Empire days.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.740
Pryde kills Hux and assumes command of the
Final Order fleet.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:00.240
Palpatine commands Pryde to show what the
Final Order is capable of by using a planet-killer

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.950
cannon on the planet Kijimi, Poe's old stomping
grounds.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.710
Palpatine doesn't actually want Rey dead.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:13.580
He wants instead to establish a new Empire
with his granddaughter as empress, after she

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.930
kills him and absorbs his Force energy.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:19.830
And, as planned, Ren doesn't succeed in killing
Rey.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:25.330
Instead, he leads Rey right to Palpatine,
and Rey discovers new layers of her own inner

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.320
darkness along the way.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:32.641
What Palpatine didn't factor into his plan
was his inability to fully draw Rey in, or

00:05:32.641 --> 00:05:37.990
Leia Organa sacrificing her own life and Force
energy to help redeem her son.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:43.230
With Rey resistant and the now-redeemed Ben
Solo ready to fight alongside her, Palpatine

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:49.240
attempts to absorb all of the Force energy
from both young Jedi to fully resurrect himself.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:54.480
It very nearly works, until Rey is able to
call down the spirits of the generations of

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.930
Jedi before her and kill Palpatine once and
for all.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:03.031
A masterfully crafted plan ultimately fails
because of kindness, determination, and the

00:06:03.031 --> 00:06:07.230
Jedi legacy proves more powerful than Palpatine's
own dark blood.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.590
"It is finished, then."

